{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement the increment on the existing Spring XD-style distributed runtime (admin server, containers, ZooKeeper coordination, pluggable message bus with RabbitMQ binder), following its established module packaging and Gradle build conventions.",
    "U1: Perform queue/topic cleanup on the container during right-to-left module undeployment rather than centrally in the admin, because only the container knows which RabbitMQ cluster the stream was deployed to; add bus-level cleanup hooks (e.g. cleanConsumer/cleanProducer) invoked by the StreamPlugin.",
    "U1: Use RabbitAdmin.getQueueProperties() to determine consumer counts and only delete a queue when the last consumer is gone; expose the feature as an optional '--clean' flag on the 'stream destroy' shell command; handle fanout exchanges/bindings by removing auto-delete exchanges and bindings after queues are removed; call the RabbitMQ management REST API directly because RabbitManagementTemplate is not yet available.",
    "U2: Introduce a stream-scoped error channel bridged from each module's error handling, published over the message bus so users can tap '<stream>.errors' to receive per-module failure messages.",
    "U3: Run a time-boxed research spike on Spring Security and Spring Boot auto-configuration, then implement HTTP basic authentication backed by externalized configuration properties for the admin REST endpoints, with credential support in the DSL shell and a basic login flow in the Admin UI; OAuth/SSO and fine-grained authorization are out of scope.",
    "U4: Identify placeholder keys by scanning the codebase (xd.stream.name, xd.job.name, xd.container.*, etc.) and document them in the reference guide; documentation only, no code changes.",
    "U5: Deliver a new MVC-aware HTTP source module running embedded Tomcat (Spring Boot based), leveraging Spring MVC content negotiation for richer content-type support and full inbound header mapping, instead of modifying the existing HTTP source module in place.",
    "U6: Implement the minimum client-side polling strategy in the shell/Admin UI for stream and job status, plus the ideal server-side event propagation using ZooKeeper watcher notifications aggregated by the admin server and pushed to connected UI clients (Server-Sent Events).",
    "U7: Build the SFTP source module on the Spring Integration SFTP inbound channel adapter, exposing standard module options (host, credentials, remote path, polling); use an embedded Apache MINA SSHD server for integration tests.",
    "U8: Build the ElasticSearch sink module on Spring Data Elasticsearch with configurable index/type and cluster settings; use an embedded ElasticSearch node for integration tests."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All work is performed by a single developer; estimates are effort in workdays (8 hours per workday), not elapsed calendar time.",
    "A working Spring XD-style codebase, build system, CI, and test conventions already exist; no greenfield setup is required beyond feature-specific test infrastructure.",
    "RabbitMQ (with the management plugin enabled) is the deployed binder and is available for development and integration testing of U1.",
    "U3 scope covers the research spike plus implementation of basic authentication for the listed REST endpoints, the DSL shell, and the Admin UI; advanced features (OAuth2, LDAP, role-based authorization) are excluded.",
    "U6 scope includes both the minimum client-side polling and the ideal server-side event propagation between containers, the admin server, and UI clients.",
    "U4 requires no code changes, only identification and documentation of available placeholder keys.",
    "Test infrastructure for U7 and U8 can rely on embeddable components (Apache MINA SSHD, embedded ElasticSearch) plus an available RabbitMQ broker for bus-level tests.",
    "The developer is experienced with Spring Integration, Spring AMQP, Spring Security, and the existing codebase; no significant ramp-up time is included.",
    "Each activity estimate includes unit tests and developer-level documentation; cross-cutting integration testing, reference documentation, and release work are estimated as separate activities.",
    "Estimates assume no major upstream API instability in the Spring portfolio dependencies during the increment."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-01",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting solution analysis and architecture",
      "activity_description": "Analyze all eight user stories, define the overall approach (container-side cleanup hooks, error channel topology, security model, event propagation), and produce lightweight design notes shared across stories.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-02",
      "activity_name": "Development and test infrastructure setup",
      "activity_description": "Provision feature-specific test infrastructure: RabbitMQ broker with management plugin, embedded Apache MINA SSHD SFTP server, embedded ElasticSearch node, and TLS/keystore artifacts for security tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-03",
      "activity_name": "U1 detailed design: stream destroy cleanup",
      "activity_description": "Design the optional queue/topic cleanup: container-side undeploy hook, last-consumer detection via RabbitAdmin.getQueueProperties(), direct RabbitMQ management REST calls, handling of non-empty queues and fanout exchanges, and the '--clean' CLI contract.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-04",
      "activity_name": "U1 implementation: stream destroy --clean",
      "activity_description": "Implement the '--clean' option on 'stream destroy', bus/StreamPlugin cleanup methods (cleanConsumer/cleanProducer), RabbitMQ REST-based queue/binding/exchange removal, and safety checks for queues with consumers or data.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-05",
      "activity_name": "U1 testing: stream destroy cleanup",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests plus integration tests against a live RabbitMQ broker covering last-consumer detection, non-empty queues, fanout exchange removal, and multi-container undeploy ordering.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-06",
      "activity_name": "U2 design and implementation: stream error channel",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a per-stream error channel: bridge module exceptions onto a bus-published '<stream>.errors' channel so failures can be tapped per stream/module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-07",
      "activity_name": "U2 testing: error channel",
      "activity_description": "Unit and integration tests verifying that module exceptions are published to the correct stream error channel and can be tapped by user modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-08",
      "activity_name": "U3 research spike: Spring Security and Boot",
      "activity_description": "Time-boxed spike researching Spring Security and Spring Boot out-of-the-box features, prototyping basic auth on an admin endpoint, and capturing findings.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-09",
      "activity_name": "U3 security design",
      "activity_description": "Define the security configuration model: externalized properties, how users configure credentials, how the DSL shell authenticates, and how the Admin UI login is handled.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-10",
      "activity_name": "U3 implementation: secured REST endpoints",
      "activity_description": "Implement the security layer wrapping all admin REST endpoints, credential configuration, shell credential support, and basic Admin UI login handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-11",
      "activity_name": "U3 testing: security",
      "activity_description": "Security-focused unit and integration tests for authenticated/unauthenticated access across REST endpoints, shell connectivity with credentials, and UI login behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-12",
      "activity_name": "U4 documentation: placeholder keys",
      "activity_description": "Identify all available placeholder keys (xd.stream.name, xd.job.name, xd.container.* and others) and document them in the reference documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-13",
      "activity_name": "U5 design and implementation: MVC-aware HTTP module",
      "activity_description": "Create a new HTTP source module with embedded Tomcat leveraging Spring MVC: richer content-type support, full inbound header mapping, and Spring Security extensibility hooks.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-14",
      "activity_name": "U5 testing: MVC HTTP module",
      "activity_description": "Unit and integration tests covering content negotiation, header mapping, concurrent requests against embedded Tomcat, and module deployment in a container.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-15",
      "activity_name": "U6 client-side polling for status changes",
      "activity_description": "Implement a common polling strategy in the shell and Admin UI to detect stream/job status changes during deployment and undeployment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-16",
      "activity_name": "U6 server-side event propagation",
      "activity_description": "Implement container-to-admin event propagation (ZooKeeper watcher based) for system state changes and push notifications from the admin server to connected UI clients via Server-Sent Events.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-17",
      "activity_name": "U6 testing: polling and event propagation",
      "activity_description": "Integration tests for polling behavior and end-to-end event flow from container state change through the admin server to UI client notification, including failure/reconnect scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-18",
      "activity_name": "U7 implementation: SFTP source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the SFTP source module based on the Spring Integration SFTP inbound adapter with standard module options (host, credentials, remote directory, polling, file filtering).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-19",
      "activity_name": "U7 testing: SFTP source",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests plus integration tests against an embedded Apache MINA SSHD server covering file transfer, polling, error handling, and stream deployment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-20",
      "activity_name": "U8 implementation: ElasticSearch sink module",
      "activity_description": "Implement the native ElasticSearch sink using Spring Data Elasticsearch with configurable index, type, cluster nodes, and payload mapping.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-21",
      "activity_name": "U8 testing: ElasticSearch sink",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests plus integration tests against an embedded ElasticSearch node covering indexing, querying of written data, and error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-22",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end system testing and regression",
      "activity_description": "Cross-feature system tests deploying complete streams/jobs that combine the new modules and features (cleanup, error channels, security, notifications) plus regression of existing functionality.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-23",
      "activity_name": "Reference documentation and user guides",
      "activity_description": "Write user-facing documentation for the new features: stream destroy --clean, error channel tapping, security configuration, MVC HTTP module, status notifications, SFTP source, and ElasticSearch sink.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
